&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Title: &amp;quot;&lt;/strong&gt;Mechanisms of Hematopoietic Fate Specification to Megakaryocytes&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Hosted by&amp;nbsp;Stavroula Kousteni, PhD,&amp;nbsp;Professor, Department of Physiology &amp;amp; Cellular Biophysics; Director, Evans MDS Center at Columbia.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This event is sponsored by the Herbert Irving Comprehensive Cancer Center&amp;#39;s (HICCC)&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href="https://www.cancer.columbia.edu/research/researchers/edward-p-evans-center-myelodysplastic-syndromes-mds" target="_blank"&gt;Edward P. Evans Center for Myelodysplastic Syndromes (MDS)&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;at Columbia University, established to&amp;nbsp;foster an all-encompassing approach in studying MDS&amp;nbsp;giving us&amp;nbsp;molecular, cellular genetic and epigenetic insights to develop and test innovative therapies.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Experts in many disciplines&amp;mdash;some working in L&amp;#39;Aquila since 2009&amp;rsquo;s catastrophic earthquake, and some involved with other post-disaster scenarios&amp;mdash;will discuss the current state of L&amp;#39;Aquila: the damaged and restored cultural heritage, the gradual revival of urban life, and the city&amp;#39;s new association with post-disaster aesthetics and construction sites.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Click&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href="https://italianacademy.columbia.edu/events/post-earthquake-reconstruction-historic-city-learning-laquila-italy"&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;to register.&lt;/p&gt;
